{
  "_about": "Slang and swear words machine translation gets wrong. Per language: 'phrases' replace a caption when the whole message is just that phrase (repeats allowed: 'есть есть' matches 'есть'); 'terms' are explained in a note under the caption wherever they appear, and a message that is nothing but one term is replaced by its meaning, like a phrase; 'replace' words are swapped for their English before a chat line is sent to the translator, so the translation itself comes out right ('с вх' gave 'with input', 'с wallhack' gives 'with wallhack') -- only for words with a clean one-word equivalent, never for insults. A trailing * matches any ending ('петух*' also catches 'петуха'). Matching ignores case, punctuation and, for Latin-script languages, accents. 'any' is checked for every message, and is meant for transliterations and shorthand that look the same in any language. Add your own in slang.json in the app's settings folder; it is merged over this one.",

